    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0155" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/5–2446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-24T18:00:00-03:00">May 24, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>972. Exchange notes on rubber, wheat still unconsummated. Argentine
                    representatives contend unable to sign until receipt new instructions
                    necessitated by resignation Sauri. Although expected daily these have not been
                    received.</p>
                <p>Brazilian Ambassador Buenos Aires<anchor n="27" xml:id="d106-f1"/> has been
                    instructed by Foreign Office to urge Argentine Government to act promptly in
                    this matter.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office has made plain that it does not wish to discuss abrogation
                    tripartite agreement at present juncture. (Department’s telegrams 551, April 25
                    and 632, May 14).<anchor n="28" xml:id="d106-f2"/> Treatment Argentina same
                    basis other countries for tire licensing has been raised and is under
                    consideration by Foreign Office; unofficial indications are there probably will
                    be no objection but Foreign Office unlikely to so state until after exchange
                    wheat, rubber notes has been effected.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
